  "_comment": "SALVAGE kit: a taped hose bundle SAGGING between two crude clamps - three cylinder segments, the outer pair tilted 5 degrees so the run dips between its supports, because a hose someone pulled taut would read as plumbing and this is not plumbing. A thinner second line runs beside it and vanishes under the tape, and the tape wraps are LIVERY GREEN: they bind with the same stolen green stock the patches are cut from, which keeps the mismatch inside the kit's three hues. Long axis Z with the clamps at 0.40 of a cell out, footprint raised to 0.92, so consecutive plates of one run join into a continuing bundle while a lone piece still reads complete - clamp, sag, clamp.",
